From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:02:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: Implement LookupPrivilegeDisplayName, and know the
 privileges Windows 11 has.

Measured on Windows 11 build 29671 with tools/privprobe (privnames.c,
tokenprivs.c):

- LUIDs go up to 36, SeDelegateSessionUserImpersonatePrivilege;
  LookupPrivilegeValue here knew none of 31 to 36.  A name that is none
  zeroes the LUID.
- LookupPrivilegeDisplayName gives the privilege's text in the user's
  language: asked for its size, the length with the terminator and
  ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER, the language already given; then the length
  without.  A name that is none is ERROR_NO_SUCH_PRIVILEGE.  The ANSI
  call asks for the wide length and gives the length in bytes.  The
  English texts are Windows', the Chinese ones as Windows has them.
- An administrator also has SeIncreaseWorkingSetPrivilege,
  SeTimeZonePrivilege, SeCreateSymbolicLinkPrivilege and
  SeDelegateSessionUserImpersonatePrivilege, disabled; enabling the
  symbolic link one now succeeds.

The test checks the new LUIDs and the display names; on Windows it has
no failures in them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

